      }, {
        "text": " component. \n\nIn this architecture, trying to simulate the `tone()` function\u0027s high-speed pin toggling cycle"
      }, {
        "text": "-by-cycle would cause heavy lag. Instead, an Active Buzzer is perfect: when you write `digitalWrite"
      }, {
        "text": "(pin, HIGH)`, the simulator will use the browser\u0027s Web Audio API to play a steady, clear beep (an"
      }, {
        "text": " 800Hz square wave) until you write `LOW`.\n\nHere is the fully updated `App.jsx"
      }, {
        "text": "` file.\n\n### How to use it in your code:\n1. Add an \"Active Buzzer\" to your"
      }, {
        "text": " robot in the Customization Lab.\n2. Set it to a pin (e.g., Pin 8)."
      }, {
        "text": "\n3. In your code, just use `digitalWrite(8, HIGH);` to start beeping, and `digitalWrite"
      }, {
