      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nI have updated the logic precisely according to the"
      }, {
        "text": " legacy specifications. \n\nHere is what I implemented to enforce the `krumon v.13071"
      }, {
        "text": "5` hardware rules:\n1.  **Console Messaging:** Toggling the mode now logs the action directly to the `SYSTEM CONSOLE"
      }, {
        "text": "`.\n2.  **Hardware Trimming:** If the user toggles Krumon Mode **ON**, the system"
      }, {
        "text": " automatically scans their current robot chassis. Any banned components (like IMU or OLED) or excess components (like a 5th DC Motor or"
      }, {
        "text": " 2nd Sonar) are immediately stripped off to guarantee a compliant build.\n3.  **Strict Dropdown Limits:** The \""
      }, {
        "text": "Add Component\" dropdown dynamically disables options once they reach the Krumon limits (Max 4 Motors, Max 7"
      }, {
        "text": " IR, Max 1 Sonar/Buzzer/Grabber/LCD).\n4.  **Pin \u0026 Position Locking:**"
      }, {
        "text": " \n    *   **DC Motors:** Pins and X/Y/Angle inputs become greyed out and uneditable.\n    *"
      }, {
        "text": "   **Buzzer, Grabber, 16x2 LCD:** Pins become greyed out, but X/Y/Angle remains editable"
      }, {
        "text": " so you can mount them anywhere.\n    *   **IR Sensors \u0026 Sonar:** Fully editable (Pins and Positions remain"
      }, {
        "text": " unlocked).\n\nHere is the updated `App.jsx`.\n\n--- START OF FILE App.jsx ---\n\n```javascript"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor"
      }, {
        "text": "/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, Grip"
      }, {
