      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nI understand"
      }, {
        "text": " exactly what went wrong. Since the position fields (`X, Y, Ang`) were locked for DC Motors, if you"
      }, {
        "text": " deleted them and added them back, they would spawn at the default `0, 0` coordinates and you had no way to move them into"
      }, {
        "text": " the wheel positions!\n\nTo fix this properly according to the `C/C++ Robot Simulator v.130715"
      }, {
        "text": "` behavior, the system should treat the core hardware as a **fixed, mandatory chassis**. \n\nHere is what I have changed"
      }, {
        "text": " in this update:\n1. **Auto-Build Chassis:** When you toggle Krumon Mode **ON**, it"
      }, {
        "text": " now automatically injects the 4 DC Motors (in exact wheel coordinates), the 1 Buzzer, the 1 Grab"
      }, {
        "text": "ber, and the 1 LCD.\n2. **Prevent Removal:** You can no longer remove these mandatory components. The"
      }, {
        "text": " \"X\" delete button is hidden for them.\n3. **Prevent Manual Addition:** Since the exact required amount of core components is automatically"
      }, {
        "text": " injected, they are completely hidden from the \"Add Component\" dropdown. You can only manually add/remove IR Sensors and the"
      }, {
        "text": " Sonar.\n\nHere is the fully updated `App.jsx`.\n\n--- START OF FILE App.jsx ---\n\n```javascript\nimport"
      }, {
