        "text": "\n\n\nGood catch."
      }, {
        "text": " I found the exact cause. \n\nWhen you clicked **\"Reset All\"**, the system was executing a strict \"Factory Sandbox"
      }, {
        "text": " Reset.\" It blindly turned `krumonMode` back to `false` and loaded the standard default robot build. This"
      }, {
        "text": " suddenly disabled all hardware limitations, which defeated the purpose of being locked into the legacy mode.\n\nI have updated the logic"
      }, {
        "text": " in `restoreDefaults` and `importConfig` so that **Krumon Mode is persistent**. \n\nIf you are currently"
      }, {
        "text": " in Krumon Mode and hit \"Reset All\":\n1. It will *stay* in Krumon Mode"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n2. It will generate a fresh, factory-clean **Krumon Chassis** (exactly 4 Motors, 1"
      }, {
        "text": " Buzzer, 1 Grabber, 1 LCD) and wipe away any extra IR/Sonar sensors you manually attached"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n3. The \"Import Config\" button has also been patched so a user cannot upload a hacked `.json` file to"
      }, {
        "text": " bypass the Krumon part limits.\n\nHere is the fully patched `App.jsx`.\n\n--- START OF FILE"
      }, {
