      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nThis is the perfect approach. By dynamically intercepting the code just before it is sent to the compiler, we can invis"
      }, {
        "text": "ibly wrap their legacy Krumon code inside a standard Arduino environment. \n\nThis means the user doesn\u0027t have to look"
      }, {
        "text": " at ugly wrapper code, and they can seamlessly compile programs written 10+ years ago.\n\nHere is what I have implemented in this update:"
      }, {
        "text": "\n1. **The Invisible Krumon Library:** Created a hidden C++ library payload that natively maps functions like `fd"
      }, {
        "text": "()`, `motor()`, `sleep()`, and `analog()` to their respective `digitalWrite` and `delay"
      }, {
        "text": "` Arduino equivalents targeting the locked Krumon chassis pins.\n2. **Include Stripper:** Automatically removes `#include \u003c"
      }, {
        "text": "krumon.h\u003e` or `\u003cpopbot.h\u003e` if the user pasted them, so the cloud compiler doesn\u0027"
      }, {
        "text": "t throw a \"file not found\" error.\n3. **Smart Entry Point Injection:** Automatically detects if the user"
      }, {
        "text": " wrote a legacy `void main()` loop. If they did, it uses a macro to safely wrap it into standard Arduino `init"
      }, {
        "text": "() -\u003e setup() -\u003e loop()` architecture without throwing Linker errors.\n4. **Krumon Default Template:** If"
      }, {
        "text": " you switch to Krumon mode, the editor automatically swaps the code out for a legacy-style `void main()` template so you can see the"
      }, {
        "text": " syntax in action immediately.\n\nHere is the fully updated `App.jsx`.\n\n--- START OF FILE App.jsx"
      }, {
        "text": " ---\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@"
      }, {
        "text": "monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings, Terminal,"
      }, {
        "text": " Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw, FileUp, ImagePlus, Trash"
      }, {
        "text": "2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027"
      }, {
        "text": "matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  AVRTimer, timer"
      }, {
        "text": "0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, usart0Config,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  AVRADC, adcConfig \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027; \n\nfunction loadHex(source,"
      }, {
        "text": " target) {\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {\n    if (line"
      }, {
        "text": "[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " parseInt(line.substring(1, 3), 16);\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line."
      }, {
        "text": "substring(3, 7), 16);\n      for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes"
      }, {
        "text": "; i++) {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line.substring(9 + i *"
      }, {
        "text": " 2, 11 + i * 2), 16);\n      }\n    }\n  }"
      }, {
        "text": "\n}\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {\n  let portAddr, bit;"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { portAddr \u003d 0x2B; bit"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d pin; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { portAddr"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d 0x25; bit \u003d pin - 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { portAddr \u003d 0x28; bit \u003d pin -"
      }, {
        "text": " 14; } \n  else { return false; }\n  return (cpu.data[portAddr]"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;\n};\n\nconst setExternalPin \u003d (cpu, pin, is"
      }, {
        "text": "High) \u003d\u003e {\n  let pinAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 7) { pinAddr \u003d 0x29; bit \u003d pin; }  \n  else if (pin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { pinAddr \u003d 0x23; bit \u003d pin -"
      }, {
        "text": " 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { pin"
      }, {
        "text": "Addr \u003d 0x26; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return;"
      }, {
        "text": " }\n\n  if (isHigh) {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c bit);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  } else {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] \u0026\u003d ~(1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  }"
      }, {
        "text": "\n};\n\nconst generateId \u003d () \u003d\u003e Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\nconst getOppositeColor \u003d (hex) \u003d\u003e {\n  if (hex.indexOf(\u0027#\u0027) \u003d\u003d\u003d 0"
      }, {
        "text": ") hex \u003d hex.slice(1);\n  if (hex.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 3) hex \u003d hex"
      }, {
        "text": "[0]+hex[0]+hex[1]+hex[1]+hex[2]+hex[2];\n  \n  let r \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(0, 2), 16);\n  let g \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(2, 4), 16);\n  let b"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(4, 6), 16);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  \n  if (Math.abs(r - 128) \u003c 30 \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(g"
      }, {
        "text": " - 128) \u003c 30 \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(b - 128) \u003c"
      }, {
        "text": " 30) {\n    return r \u003e 128 ? \u0027#000000\u0027 : \u0027#"
      }, {
        "text": "ffffff\u0027;\n  }\n  \n  return `#${r.toString(16).padStart(2, \u0027"
      }, {
        "text": "0\u0027)}${g.toString(16).padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}${b.toString(16"
      }, {
        "text": ").padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}`;\n};\n\nconst TYPE_TAGS \u003d {\n  dc_motor"
      }, {
        "text": ": \u0027DC MOTOR\u0027,\n  imu: \u0027IMU\u0027,\n  ir_sensor: \u0027IR SENSOR\u0027,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  sonar: \u0027SONAR\u0027,\n  grabber: \u0027GRABBER\u0027,\n  buzzer: \u0027"
      }, {
        "text": "BUZZER\u0027,\n  oled128x64: \u0027128x64 OLED\u0027,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  lcd16x2: \u002716x2 LCD\u0027\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_COLORS \u003d {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  chassis: \u0027#3b82f6\u0027,\n  dc_motor: \u0027#00000"
      }, {
        "text": "0\u0027,\n  sonar: \u0027#ef4444\u0027,\n  ir_sensor: \u0027#22c5"
      }, {
        "text": "5e\u0027,\n  grabber: \u0027#06b6d4\u0027,\n  buzzer: \u0027#f5"
      }, {
        "text": "9e0b\u0027,\n  imu: \u0027#a855f7\u0027,\n  lcd16x2"
      }, {
        "text": ": \u0027#84cc16\u0027,\n  oled128x64: \u0027#0ea5e9"
      }, {
        "text": "\u0027,\n  arena_static: \u0027#52525b\u0027,\n  arena_prop: \u0027#a8"
      }, {
        "text": "55f7\u0027\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_CONFIG \u003d {\n  leftWidth: 45,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  editorHeight: 60,\n  canvasHeight: 65,\n  customLabWidth:"
      }, {
        "text": " 66,\n  robotX: 200,\n  robotY: 250,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  robotAngle: 0,\n  baudRate: \"9600\",\n  krumonMode"
      }, {
        "text": ": false,\n  robotBuild: {\n    chassisW: 50,\n    chassisH"
      }, {
        "text": ": 30,\n    chassisColor: DEFAULT_COLORS.chassis,\n    parts:"
