      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nThis is a very clever and practical compromise. By intercepting a specific string tag"
      }, {
        "text": " (like `[LCD]`) in the standard Serial Monitor output, we can \"hijack\" that text and route it directly to the virtual"
      }, {
        "text": " LCD/OLED display UI without needing to simulate complex I2C clock cycles. \n\nHere is what I implemented"
      }, {
        "text": " in this update:\n1.  **Serial Interception:** The internal serial reader now watches for any line starting with `[LCD]`."
      }, {
        "text": "\n2.  **Krumon Lib Upgrade:** I updated the hidden Krumon compatibility library. The legacy `lcd(format, ...)` function"
      }, {
        "text": " now uses `vsnprintf` to format your text, and sends it to the serial monitor as `[LCD]Your Text`."
      }, {
        "text": " \n3.  **Newline Support:** If Krumon code uses `\\n` to split lines (e"
      }, {
        "text": ".g., `lcd(\"Line1\\nLine2\")`), the C library escapes it and the React UI parses"
      }, {
        "text": " it perfectly so it correctly renders on two lines on the UI display.\n4.  **Standard Mode Bonus:** Even"
      }, {
        "text": " if you turn Krumon Mode off, you can now write `Serial.println(\"[LCD]Hello World\");` in standard"
      }, {
        "text": " Arduino code, and it will magically appear on the virtual screen components!\n\nHere is the fully updated `App.jsx`.\n\n--- START OF"
      }, {
        "text": " FILE App.jsx ---\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": "\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCcw, Monitor,"
      }, {
        "text": " Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw, FileUp,"
      }, {
        "text": " ImagePlus, Trash2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js"
      }, {
        "text": "\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction, \n  AVRTimer, timer0Config,"
      }, {
        "text": " timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVRUSART, usart0Config,\n  AVR"
      }, {
        "text": "ADC, adcConfig \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027; \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027)) {\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u002700\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line"
      }, {
        "text": ".substring(1, 3), 16);\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3"
      }, {
        "text": ", 7), 16);\n      for (let i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++)"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line.substring(9 + i * 2,"
      }, {
        "text": " 11 + i * 2), 16);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {\n  let portAddr, bit;\n  if ("
      }, {
        "text": "pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { portAddr \u003d 0x2B; bit \u003d pin;"
      }, {
        "text": " } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { portAddr \u003d 0"
      }, {
        "text": "x25; bit \u003d pin - 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026"
      }, {
        "text": " pin \u003c\u003d 19) { portAddr \u003d 0x28; bit \u003d pin - 14;"
      }, {
        "text": " } \n  else { return false; }\n  return (cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;\n};\n\nconst setExternalPin \u003d (cpu, pin, isHigh) \u003d\u003e"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n  let pinAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) {"
      }, {
        "text": " pinAddr \u003d 0x29; bit \u003d pin; }  \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { pinAddr \u003d 0x23; bit \u003d pin - 8;"
      }, {
        "text": " } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { pinAddr \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 0x26; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return; }"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n  if (isHigh) {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] |\u003d (1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  }"
      }, {
        "text": " else {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] \u0026\u003d ~(1 \u003c\u003c bit);\n  }\n};\n\nconst"
      }, {
        "text": " generateId \u003d () \u003d\u003e Math.random().toString(36).substr(2, 9);\n\nconst get"
      }, {
        "text": "OppositeColor \u003d (hex) \u003d\u003e {\n  if (hex.indexOf(\u0027#\u0027) \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) hex \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " hex.slice(1);\n  if (hex.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 3) hex \u003d hex[0]+hex"
      }, {
        "text": "[0]+hex[1]+hex[1]+hex[2]+hex[2];\n  \n  let r \u003d 255"
      }, {
        "text": " - parseInt(hex.slice(0, 2), 16);\n  let g \u003d 25"
      }, {
        "text": "5 - parseInt(hex.slice(2, 4), 16);\n  let b \u003d 2"
      }, {
        "text": "55 - parseInt(hex.slice(4, 6), 16);\n  \n  if ("
      }, {
        "text": "Math.abs(r - 128) \u003c 30 \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(g - 1"
      }, {
        "text": "28) \u003c 30 \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(b - 128) \u003c 30)"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n    return r \u003e 128 ? \u0027#000000\u0027 : \u0027#ffffff\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  }\n  \n  return `#${r.toString(16).padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}${"
      }, {
        "text": "g.toString(16).padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}${b.toString(16).padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}`;"
      }, {
        "text": "\n};\n\nconst TYPE_TAGS \u003d {\n  dc_motor: \u0027DC MOTOR\u0027,\n  imu:"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0027IMU\u0027,\n  ir_sensor: \u0027IR SENSOR\u0027,\n  sonar: \u0027SONAR\u0027,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  grabber: \u0027GRABBER\u0027,\n  buzzer: \u0027BUZZER\u0027,\n  oled12"
      }, {
        "text": "8x64: \u0027128x64 OLED\u0027,\n  lcd16x2: \u00271"
      }, {
        "text": "6x2 LCD\u0027\n};\n\nconst DEFAULT_COLORS \u003d {\n  chassis: \u0027#3b82"
      }, {
        "text": "f6\u0027,\n  dc_motor: \u0027#000000\u0027,\n  sonar: \u0027#ef4"
      }, {
        "text": "444\u0027,\n  ir_sensor: \u0027#22c55e\u0027,\n  grabber: \u0027#"
      }, {
        "text": "06b6d4\u0027,\n  buzzer: \u0027#f59e0b\u0027,\n  imu:"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0027#a855f7\u0027,\n  lcd16x2: \u0027#84cc16\u0027,"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  oled128x64: \u0027#0ea5e9\u0027,\n  arena_static: \u0027#5"
      }, {
        "text": "2525b\u0027,\n  arena_prop: \u0027#a855f7\u0027\n};\n\nconst"
      }, {
