      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\n\nYes, we absolutely can! And"
      }, {
        "text": " it is highly realistic to do so. \n\nInstead of just checking if the pin is `HIGH` or `LOW` digitally"
      }, {
        "text": ", we can tap directly into the ATmega328P\u0027s internal **Hardware Timer Registers** inside the AVR8js CPU"
      }, {
        "text": ". When you use `analogWrite()` in Arduino, it enables Pulse Width Modulation (PWM) on specific pins (3"
      }, {
        "text": ", 5, 6, 9, 10, 11) by setting a value from 0-"
      }, {
        "text": "255 in the `OCR` (Output Compare Register).\n\nI have written a new `getPinPWM` function that reads"
      }, {
        "text": " these exact memory addresses in the virtual silicon. This means your virtual motors now accept proportional speed/power!\n\nHere is what"
      }, {
        "text": " I changed in this update:\n1.  **Analog Motor Physics:** The DC Motor force is now multiplied by a `power` variable (0"
      }, {
        "text": ".0 to 1.0) derived from the PWM register (0 to 255).\n2.  **Analog UI Indicators"
      }, {
        "text": ":** The green `●` indicator next to the DC motors in the Customization Lab will now fade and brighten based on the PWM power level,"
      }, {
        "text": " giving you a visual cue of analog speed.\n3.  **Krumon Lib Update:** The invisible Krumon functions (`fd`,"
      }, {
        "text": " `sl`, `sr`, `tl`, `tr`, `motor`) have been upgraded to use `analogWrite` instead of"
      }, {
        "text": " `digitalWrite`. So `fd(50)` will now apply exactly 50% power to the virtual physics"
      }, {
        "text": " motors.\n4.  **Standard Template Update:** The standard Arduino default code has been updated to use `analogWrite("
      }, {
        "text": "MOTOR_LEFT, 128)` to showcase the new analog capability.\n\n*(Note: Because a DC Motor component"
      }, {
        "text": " is physically a single wire, it can only go forward or stop. `bk()` will stop it. If you want reverse, you\u0027d"
      }, {
        "text": " have to build an H-bridge chassis with backward-facing motors!)*\n\nHere is the fully updated `App.jsx`."
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n--- START OF FILE App.jsx ---\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCc"
      }, {
        "text": "w, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw"
      }, {
        "text": ", FileUp, ImagePlus, Trash2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide"
      }, {
        "text": "-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction,"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  AVRTimer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVR"
      }, {
        "text": "USART, usart0Config,\n  AVRADC, adcConfig \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": " \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027))"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u00270"
      }, {
        "text": "0\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring(1, 3), 16);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7), 16);\n      for (let"
      }, {
        "text": " i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line"
      }, {
        "text": ".substring(9 + i * 2, 11 + i * 2), 16);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  let portAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { portAddr"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d 0x2B; bit \u003d pin; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003d 13) { portAddr \u003d 0x25; bit \u003d pin - 8; }"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { portAddr \u003d 0x"
      }, {
        "text": "28; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return false; }\n  return"
      }, {
        "text": " (cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;\n};\n\n// Directly read"
      }, {
        "text": " the ATmega328P Timer Output Compare Registers (OCR) for precise Analog/PWM values\nconst getPinPWM"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {\n  if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 3) {\n    if (cpu."
      }, {
        "text": "data[0xB0] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 5)) return cpu.data[0xB4]; // T"
      }, {
        "text": "CCR2A \u0026 COM2B1 -\u003e OCR2B\n  } else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 5) {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n    if (cpu.data[0x44] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 5)) return cpu.data"
      }, {
        "text": "[0x48]; // TCCR0A \u0026 COM0B1 -\u003e OCR0B\n  } else"
      }, {
        "text": " if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 6) {\n    if (cpu.data[0x44] \u0026 (1"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003c 7)) return cpu.data[0x47]; // TCCR0A \u0026 COM0A1"
      }, {
        "text": " -\u003e OCR0A\n  } else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 9) {\n    if (cpu.data"
      }, {
        "text": "[0x80] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 7)) return cpu.data[0x88]; // T"
      }, {
        "text": "CCR1A \u0026 COM1A1 -\u003e OCR1AL\n  } else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 10)"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n    if (cpu.data[0x80] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 5)) return cpu."
      }, {
        "text": "data[0x8A]; // TCCR1A \u0026 COM1B1 -\u003e OCR1BL\n  }"
      }, {
        "text": " else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 11) {\n    if (cpu.data[0xB0] \u0026 ("
      }, {
        "text": "1 \u003c\u003c 7)) return cpu.data[0xB3]; // TCCR2A \u0026 COM2A1"
      }, {
        "text": " -\u003e OCR2A\n  }\n  // Fallback to digital reading if PWM is not active on the pin\n  return getPinState("
      }, {
        "text": "cpu, pin) ? 255 : 0;\n};\n\nconst setExternalPin \u003d (cpu,"
      }, {
        "text": " pin, isHigh) \u003d\u003e {\n  let pinAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026"
      }, {
        "text": " pin \u003c\u003d 7) { pinAddr \u003d 0x29; bit \u003d pin; }  \n  else"
      }, {
        "text": " if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { pinAddr \u003d 0x23; bit"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d pin - 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19"
      }, {
        "text": ") { pinAddr \u003d 0x26; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else"
      }, {
        "text": " { return; }\n\n  if (isHigh) {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] |\u003d (1"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003c bit);\n  } else {\n    cpu.data[pinAddr] \u0026\u003d ~(1 \u003c\u003c bit);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  }\n};\n\nconst generateId \u003d () \u003d\u003e Math.random().toString(36).substr(2,"
      }, {
        "text": " 9);\n\nconst getOppositeColor \u003d (hex) \u003d\u003e {\n  if (hex.indexOf(\u0027#\u0027)"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d\u003d\u003d 0) hex \u003d hex.slice(1);\n  if (hex.length \u003d\u003d\u003d 3) hex"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d hex[0]+hex[0]+hex[1]+hex[1]+hex[2]+hex[2];"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  \n  let r \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(0, 2),"
      }, {
        "text": " 16);\n  let g \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(2, 4),"
      }, {
        "text": " 16);\n  let b \u003d 255 - parseInt(hex.slice(4, 6"
      }, {
        "text": "), 16);\n  \n  if (Math.abs(r - 128) \u003c"
      }, {
        "text": " 30 \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(g - 128) \u003c 30 \u0026\u0026 Math.abs(b"
      }, {
        "text": " - 128) \u003c 30) {\n    return r \u003e 128 ? \u0027#0"
      }, {
        "text": "00000\u0027 : \u0027#ffffff\u0027;\n  }\n  \n  return `#${r.toString("
      }, {
        "text": "16).padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}${g.toString(16).padStart(2, \u00270"
      }, {
        "text": "\u0027)}${b.toString(16).padStart(2, \u00270\u0027)}`;\n};\n\nconst TYPE_TAG"
      }, {
        "text": "S \u003d {\n  dc_motor: \u0027DC MOTOR\u0027,\n  imu: \u0027IMU\u0027,\n  ir"
