        "text": "\n\n\nYou are completely right to call"
      }, {
        "text": " that out! A robot simulator isn\u0027t much good if it can\u0027t go backward. \n\nThe issue was that our"
      }, {
        "text": " virtual DC Motors were only wired with a **single pin** (PWM/Speed). In real hardware, a motor driver (like an L298"
      }, {
        "text": "N or TB6612) requires **two pins per motor**: one for Speed (PWM) and one for Direction (HIGH"
      }, {
        "text": "/LOW). \n\nI have upgraded the DC Motor component to act like a real motor driver. \n\nHere is"
      }, {
        "text": " what I changed in this update:\n1. **Direction Pins Added:** DC Motors now have a `Dir` pin alongside"
      }, {
        "text": " their `PWM` pin. By default, Left Motors use `Dir: 7` and Right Motors use `Dir: 4`.\n2"
      }, {
        "text": ". **Krumon Library Upgraded:** The invisible library now perfectly maps `bk()`, `sl()` (Spin"
      }, {
        "text": " Left), `sr()` (Spin Right), and `motor(1, -50)` (negative speed) to toggle these direction"
      }, {
        "text": " pins. \n3. **Red Reverse Indicators:** In the Customization Lab UI, the green `●` motor"
      }, {
        "text": " indicator will now turn **Red** when the motor is running in reverse, so you can visually debug your spins and backups"
      }, {
        "text": "!\n4. **Templates Updated:** Both the standard Arduino template and the Krumon template have been updated to demonstrate"
      }, {
        "text": " reversing `bk()`.\n\nHere is the fully updated `App.jsx`. Your `bk()` code will now drive"
      }, {
        "text": " the robot backward!\n\n--- START OF FILE App.jsx ---\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef"
      }, {
        "text": ", useEffect } from \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play,"
      }, {
        "text": " Square, RotateCcw, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload"
      }, {
        "text": ", RefreshCcw, FileUp, ImagePlus, Trash2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box }"
      }, {
        "text": " from \u0027lucide-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU,"
      }, {
        "text": " avrInstruction, \n  AVRTimer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config,"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  AVRUSART, usart0Config,\n  AVRADC, adcConfig \n} from \u0027"
      }, {
        "text": "avr8js\u0027; \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of source."
      }, {
