      "parts": [{
        "text": "\n\n\nThis is a hilarious and classic Arduino problem! You just ran into a 15-year-old C++"
      }, {
        "text": " naming collision.\n\n### Why it failed:\nBy default, the core Arduino compiler includes a hidden file called `binary.h`. This file contains shortcuts"
      }, {
        "text": " for writing binary numbers, like:\n```cpp\n#define B0 0\n#define B1 1\n#define B10"
      }, {
        "text": " 2\n#define B11 3\n// ... etc\n```\nWhen you wrote `int B1, B2..."
      }, {
        "text": " B10, B11;`, the compiler secretly replaced your variable names with raw numbers before it even tried to compile. Your code essentially looked"
      }, {
        "text": " like `int 1, B2, B3... 2, 3;`, which caused a massive syntax error!"
      }, {
        "text": "\n\n### The Missing Function:\nYour code also called `system_stop()`, which was a Popbot/Krumon specific"
      }, {
        "text": " library function used to freeze the CPU forever.\n\n### The Fix:\nI have updated the invisible Krumon payload"
      }, {
        "text": ". \n1. It now strictly disables the Arduino `binary.h` library by declaring a dummy `#define Binary_h` header"
      }, {
        "text": " guard. This frees up `B1`, `B10`, `B11`, etc., so you can use them as normal variables"
      }, {
        "text": ".\n2. I added the missing `void system_stop()` function. It now properly executes `ao();` ("
      }, {
        "text": "all off) and then traps the CPU in an infinite `while(1)` loop, mirroring the real hardware behavior perfectly.\n\nHere is the"
      }, {
        "text": " fully patched `App.jsx`.\n\n--- START OF FILE App.jsx ---\n\n```javascript\nimport React, { useState, useRef, useEffect } from"
      }, {
        "text": " \u0027react\u0027;\nimport Editor from \u0027@monaco-editor/react\u0027;\nimport { Play, Square, RotateCc"
      }, {
        "text": "w, Monitor, Settings, Terminal, Crosshair, GripVertical, GripHorizontal, Download, Upload, RefreshCcw"
      }, {
        "text": ", FileUp, ImagePlus, Trash2, Wrench, PlusCircle, X, Box } from \u0027lucide"
      }, {
        "text": "-react\u0027;\nimport Matter from \u0027matter-js\u0027;\nimport { \n  CPU, avrInstruction,"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  AVRTimer, timer0Config, timer1Config, timer2Config, \n  AVR"
      }, {
        "text": "USART, usart0Config,\n  AVRADC, adcConfig \n} from \u0027avr8js\u0027;"
      }, {
        "text": " \n\nfunction loadHex(source, target) {\n  for (const line of source.split(\u0027\\n\u0027))"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n    if (line[0] \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027:\u0027 \u0026\u0026 line.substring(7, 9) \u003d\u003d\u003d \u00270"
      }, {
        "text": "0\u0027) {\n      const bytes \u003d parseInt(line.substring(1, 3), 16);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n      const addr \u003d parseInt(line.substring(3, 7), 16);\n      for (let"
      }, {
        "text": " i \u003d 0; i \u003c bytes; i++) {\n        target[addr + i] \u003d parseInt(line"
      }, {
        "text": ".substring(9 + i * 2, 11 + i * 2), 16);"
      }, {
        "text": "\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\nconst getPinState \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  let portAddr, bit;\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { portAddr"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003d 0x2B; bit \u003d pin; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin"
      }, {
        "text": " \u003c\u003d 13) { portAddr \u003d 0x25; bit \u003d pin - 8; }"
      }, {
        "text": " \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 14 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { portAddr \u003d 0x"
      }, {
        "text": "28; bit \u003d pin - 14; } \n  else { return false; }\n  return"
      }, {
        "text": " (cpu.data[portAddr] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c bit)) !\u003d\u003d 0;\n};\n\n// Directly read"
      }, {
        "text": " the ATmega328P Timer Output Compare Registers (OCR) for precise Analog/PWM values\nconst getPin"
      }, {
        "text": "PWM \u003d (cpu, pin) \u003d\u003e {\n  if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 3) {\n    if (cpu"
      }, {
        "text": ".data[0xB0] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 5)) return cpu.data[0xB4]; //"
      }, {
        "text": " TCCR2A \u0026 COM2B1 -\u003e OCR2B\n  } else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 5)"
      }, {
        "text": " {\n    if (cpu.data[0x44] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 5)) return cpu."
      }, {
        "text": "data[0x48]; // TCCR0A \u0026 COM0B1 -\u003e OCR0B\n  }"
      }, {
        "text": " else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 6) {\n    if (cpu.data[0x44] \u0026 ("
      }, {
        "text": "1 \u003c\u003c 7)) return cpu.data[0x47]; // TCCR0A \u0026 COM0A"
      }, {
        "text": "1 -\u003e OCR0A\n  } else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 9) {\n    if (cpu.data"
      }, {
        "text": "[0x80] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 7)) return cpu.data[0x88]; //"
      }, {
        "text": " TCCR1A \u0026 COM1A1 -\u003e OCR1AL\n  } else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 10"
      }, {
        "text": ") {\n    if (cpu.data[0x80] \u0026 (1 \u003c\u003c 5)) return cpu"
      }, {
        "text": ".data[0x8A]; // TCCR1A \u0026 COM1B1 -\u003e OCR1BL"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  } else if (pin \u003d\u003d\u003d 11) {\n    if (cpu.data[0xB0] \u0026"
      }, {
        "text": " (1 \u003c\u003c 7)) return cpu.data[0xB3]; // TCCR2A \u0026 COM2A"
      }, {
        "text": "1 -\u003e OCR2A\n  }\n  // Fallback to digital reading if PWM is not active on the pin"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  return getPinState(cpu, pin) ? 255 : 0;\n};\n\nconst"
      }, {
        "text": " setExternalPin \u003d (cpu, pin, isHigh) \u003d\u003e {\n  let pinAddr, bit;"
      }, {
        "text": "\n  if (pin \u003e\u003d 0 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 7) { pinAddr \u003d 0x29; bit \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " pin; }  \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 8 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 13) { pinAddr \u003d"
      }, {
        "text": " 0x23; bit \u003d pin - 8; } \n  else if (pin \u003e\u003d 1"
      }, {
        "text": "4 \u0026\u0026 pin \u003c\u003d 19) { pinAddr \u003d 0x26; bit \u003d pin - 1"
      }, {
        "text": "4; } \n  else { return; }\n\n  if (isHigh) {\n    cpu.data"
      }, {
